<title>USA: Troy, N.Y., gets extension on repaying state loan.</title>
<headline>Troy, N.Y., gets extension on repaying state loan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Troy, N.Y., which is struggling to repair its finances, is getting an extension on repaying a $16 million dollar state loan.</p>
<p>The new deadline is November 26.</p>
<p>State Comptroller H. Carl McCall said that the extension is just a housekeeping move because Troy is still negotiating for a refinancing package.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
